**Recommendation: Redis Streams** — the binding constraints make this clear. Redis is already in the stack, the team has zero Kafka experience, the 2-week delivery window rules out learning and operating a new distributed system, and our throughput (5,000 req/s at 10× growth) is two orders of magnitude below where Kafka's advantages matter. Exactly-once for billing notifications is achievable via a PostgreSQL dedup table — the same pattern used by Stripe and Shopify over at-least-once transports.

Kafka would be the right call if throughput scaled past ~100k msg/s, if we needed multi-datacenter replication, or if we had a dedicated platform engineering team. None of those are true today.
